<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<Description>Dynamic filtering, sorting and paging for IQueryable, driven by data rather than code. A condition built in code, parsed from a compact query language, or deserialized from a client becomes an expression tree and is applied to a query. You declare which properties are filterable, and callers can filter on those and nothing else. Works with EF Core, where conditions become SQL with values passed as parameters, and in memory over the same data. No dependencies.</Description>
		<PackageTags>iqueryable;linq;efcore;entity-framework-core;filtering;sorting;paging;expression-trees;dynamic-query;query-language</PackageTags>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
Weequery 3.0.0. A large release; the README covers all of it.

BREAKING. Inquiry is immutable. ApplyCondition, ApplySorts and every Bind call return a new Inquiry rather than
changing the one they were called on, so a configured Inquiry can be kept and branched and neither branch can
reach the other. A chain that discards the return value no longer accumulates anything.

BREAKING. QueryStyle.Native is the default for reading and writing query strings. QueryStyle.CSharp and
QueryStyle.Sql are deprecated and will be removed in 4.0; pass one explicitly to keep the old spelling.

Added: binding resolution, so BindResolve walks the entity and binds what it finds, with
BindingResolutionSettings to subtract before it does. Collections, with BindCollection and Any, All and None
over their elements. Projection, so a caller chooses the columns as well as the rows, with * and Prefix.*
wildcards. Paging, through BuildPaged and PagedQuery. BindingUse, so filtering, sorting and projection are
granted separately and RemoveBinding revokes any of them, by name or by wildcard. ListBindings, which reads the
allow-list back so you can see what resolution opened up. Validate, which reports what a query would do before
it runs. InquirySettings.IgnoreUnboundFields, which drops what it cannot bind rather than refusing the query and
reports it in DroppedFields. QueryRequest, carrying filter, sort, projection and paging in one object. A
WeequeryError code on every refusal. Value conversion, per-backend operator support, and trimming and Native AOT
annotations throughout.

Companion packages for EF Core, OData, Elasticsearch, AutoMapper, Mapster and Mapperly are released alongside at
the same version.
		</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

